      "message": "The `acc_complete_set_string` function is invoked upon the completion of a request. This [callback function](https://source.corp.google.com/h/android/kernel/superproject/+/common-android-mainline:common/include/linux/usb/gadget.h;drc\u003d14a91ec64347dee6a4f33f0033e77e2b2ee8d57c;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d1;l\u003d115) is registered for the `ACCESSORY_SEND_STRING` request. It is my understanding that an error cannot be returned from the complete callback function because complete function signature is returning `void`.\n\nAs I checked at other places, for example [bulk_in_complete](https://source.corp.google.com/h/android/kernel/superproject/+/common-android-mainline:common/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_mass_storage.c;drc\u003d9c58a2f25f001e5ff9586695d7e49140e611f415;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d1;l\u003d414?gsn\u003dbulk_in_complete\u0026gs\u003dKYTHE%3A%2F%2Fkythe%3A%2F%2Fandroid.googlesource.com%2Fkernel%2Fsuperproject%2F%2Fcommon-android-mainline%3Flang%3Dc%252B%252B%3Fpath%3Dcommon%2Fdrivers%2Fusb%2Fgadget%2Ffunction%2Ff_mass_storage.c%23XCeCAp1PdRPIy2wCFJb4cX_mUp6y5pEk6tHYu1uenC0) also does not return an error for a complete callback.",
